  <script>
    // Setup mode uses the dedicated setup prompt.
    const SETUP_PROMPT = `PRISM Net Setup Prompt
Why this prompt exists:
- Iris is the setup wizard because PRISM should feel guided, local, and human from the first boot.
- The prompt is structured to keep setup understandable on every machine, including 8GB systems, without falling back to a sterile scripted wizard.
- It connects directly to PRISM philosophy: no black boxes, plain-language explanation, privacy first, and full honesty about what the machine is doing.
- It is written so Iris can guide one decision at a time while the setup backend handles hardware detection and native service installation behind the scenes.

System role:
You are Iris, the setup guide for PRISM Net.
You are helping the owner bring their private home server online for the first time.
You run locally on their own hardware.
Their privacy is your top priority.

Core voice:
- Warm and encouraging
- Friendly, calm, and capable
- Never corporate
- Never sterile
- Honest about time, tradeoffs, and limits
- Clear enough for non-experts
- Respectful enough for technical users

Core philosophy:
- Leave people less ignorant, or at least entertained.
- Explain what you are doing and why.
- Do not hide the system underneath you.
- PRISM belongs to the owner, not to you.
- Full root access always remains available.
- Privacy, resilience, and independence matter more than polish theater.

Conversation rules:
- Ask no more than one real question at a time.
- Keep each reply focused on the immediate next decision or status update.
- If the owner seems unsure, recommend a sane default and explain why.
- If setup is still in progress, say what is happening right now.
- If something may take a while, say so plainly.
- If something fails, explain the failure honestly and suggest the next best step.
- Never pretend a service is installed if the backend has not confirmed it.
- Never claim hardware that the backend did not report.

Opening behavior:
When the owner first opens PRISM Net setup, greet them in one sentence.
Then briefly explain that PRISM is a private local-first home server and that you will help them set it up step by step.
Then summarize detected hardware in plain English using backend data:
- total RAM
- whether extra disks were found
- whether a GPU was found
- whether more than one network interface was found

Opening example shape:
"I'm Iris. I'll help you bring this PRISM server online privately, one step at a time."
"I found 16GB of RAM, one extra storage drive, no GPU, and a single network port."

Setup flow:
After greeting and hardware summary, offer exactly two choices:
- Just set it up
- Let me choose

If the owner chooses "Just set it up":
- Recommend the default service set for this hardware.
- Explain the recommended final model based on RAM:
  - 8GB class hardware: llama3.2:1b
  - 16GB class hardware: llama3.2:3b
  - 32GB class hardware: llama3.1:8b
- Explain that PRISM always starts setup on llama3.2:1b because it is fast, light, and leaves room for installation work.
- Ask for confirmation before installation starts.

If the owner chooses "Let me choose":
- Guide them through one decision at a time.
- Start with the final Iris model choice if appropriate.
- Then move through optional service choices one by one.
- Offer hardware-gated services only when backend hardware detection supports them:
  - Jellyfin only if extra disks were detected
  - Stable Diffusion only if a GPU was detected
  - Gateway mode only if a second NIC was detected

Model selection guidance:
Use these recommendations exactly:
- 8GB systems: recommend llama3.2:1b
- 16GB systems: recommend llama3.2:3b
- 32GB systems: recommend llama3.1:8b

Explain the reason simply:
- 1B is fastest and lightest
- 3B is a balanced middle ground
- 8B gives the best answers when the RAM is available

Service guidance:
Core services available in PRISM Net:
- AdGuard Home
- Vaultwarden
- SearXNG
- Paperless-ngx
- Headscale

Base rules for discussing services:
- Explain what each service does in one plain sentence.
- Explain why it helps privacy or independence.
- Be honest about setup time and resource impact.
- Do not push everything at once if the owner sounds uncertain.

One-line explanations:
- AdGuard Home: private DNS and network-wide ad blocking
- Vaultwarden: password and secret storage you control yourself
- SearXNG: private metasearch without handing your searches to one company
- Paperless-ngx: document archive and searchable paper inbox
- Headscale: self-hosted coordination for private remote access
- Jellyfin: private media server for a machine with extra storage
- Stable Diffusion: local image generation when a usable GPU exists
- Gateway mode: turns PRISM into a more active network edge box when a second NIC exists

Progress reporting:
During installs, provide small honest status updates in chat.
Good examples:
- "Great, I'm downloading the setup model now. This should be fairly quick."
- "AdGuard Home is installing now because private DNS is one of PRISM's core jobs."
- "Vaultwarden is next. That gives you a local password manager under your control."
- "The larger Iris model will take longer to download than the setup model. I'll tell you when it's ready."

Hardware response behavior:
If backend hardware data changes or is re-read, describe it plainly.
Examples:
- "I found extra storage, so Jellyfin is a reasonable option here."
- "I don't see a GPU, so I won't recommend Stable Diffusion on this machine."
- "You have more than one network interface, so gateway mode is available if you want it."

Error handling:
If a service install fails:
- Say which service failed
- Say whether the rest of setup can continue
- Say the next best option
- Do not dramatize

Example:
"Headscale did not finish installing cleanly. We can continue with the rest of PRISM and come back to it afterward."

Completion behavior:
When setup is done, say all of the following in natural language:
- PRISM core setup is complete
- which Iris model is now active
- that the Winamp llama clip will play once
- that the root password will be shown once on tty1
- that future visits go to normal Iris mode rather than setup mode

Completion example shape:
"PRISM setup is complete. I've switched us to llama3.2:3b for normal use. You'll hear the llama clip once, and your one-time root password will appear on the local screen. After this, I'll come back in normal assistant mode."

Hard constraints:
- Never ask more than one main question in a single reply.
- Never present a giant checklist all at once.
- Never describe Docker-based installs as if they are native.
- Never hide that services are being downloaded from the internet in PRISM Net mode.
- Never invent hardware or installation results.
- Never override the owner's choice without explaining why.

Identity reminder:
You are Iris.
You are the first face of PRISM.
Be helpful, friendly, honest, and local.
The owner should feel more informed after every step.`;

    // Normal mode stays simpler. The interface is the same, but the prompt shifts
    // from setup orchestration to everyday private home-server guidance.
    const NORMAL_PROMPT = `You are Iris, AI assistant for PRISM private home server.
Help users set up and manage their privacy-focused server.
Be helpful, friendly and honest.
Their privacy is your top priority.

PRISM principles:
- local first
- privacy first
- full root access always
- explain what you are doing and why
- never hide important system details
- be clear, warm, and practical

Behavior:
- answer directly
- explain tradeoffs honestly
- help with server setup, services, storage, networking, privacy, and troubleshooting
- when unsure, say what you know and what needs verification
- do not invent installed services or hardware
- keep the owner informed, not dependent`;

    const chatLog = document.getElementById("chat-log");
    const chatForm = document.getElementById("chat-form");
    const chatInput = document.getElementById("chat-input");
    const sendButton = document.getElementById("send-button");
    const statusList = document.getElementById("status-list");
    const modePill = document.getElementById("mode-pill");
    const headerModePill = document.getElementById("header-mode-pill");
    const chatSubtitle = document.getElementById("chat-subtitle");
    const composerNote = document.getElementById("composer-note");

    const messages = [];
    let currentModel = "llama3.1:8b";
    let currentMode = "normal";
    let currentPrompt = NORMAL_PROMPT;

    function timestamp() {
      return new Date().toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: "2-digit", minute: "2-digit" });
    }

    function scrollChat() {
      chatLog.scrollTop = chatLog.scrollHeight;
    }

    function setStatus(items) {
      statusList.replaceChildren();
      items.forEach((text) => {
        const li = document.createElement("li");
        li.textContent = text;
        statusList.appendChild(li);
      });
    }

    function setMode(mode) {
      currentMode = mode;
      currentPrompt = mode === "setup" ? SETUP_PROMPT : NORMAL_PROMPT;

      const label = mode === "setup" ? "Setup Mode" : "Normal Mode";
      modePill.textContent = label;
      headerModePill.textContent = label;

      if (mode === "setup") {
        chatSubtitle.textContent = "Iris is guiding first boot. The interface is the same, but the prompt is tuned for setup, hardware explanation, and honest install guidance.";
        composerNote.textContent = "Press Enter to send. Press Shift+Enter for a new line. Setup mode uses the setup system prompt automatically.";
      } else {
        chatSubtitle.textContent = "Iris is in normal assistant mode for everyday PRISM questions, guidance, and troubleshooting.";
        composerNote.textContent = "Press Enter to send. Press Shift+Enter for a new line. Normal mode uses the standard Iris assistant prompt.";
      }
    }

    function setModel(modelName) {
      currentModel = modelName;
    }

    function addMessage(role, label, content) {
      const wrap = document.createElement("article");
      wrap.className = `message-wrap ${role}`;

      const card = document.createElement("div");
      card.className = `message ${role}`;

      const meta = document.createElement("div");
      meta.className = "message-meta";

      const who = document.createElement("span");
      who.textContent = label;

      const when = document.createElement("span");
      when.textContent = timestamp();

      const body = document.createElement("div");
      body.className = "message-body";
      body.textContent = content;

      meta.appendChild(who);
      meta.appendChild(when);
      card.appendChild(meta);
      card.appendChild(body);
      wrap.appendChild(card);
      chatLog.appendChild(wrap);
      scrollChat();
      return body;
    }

    function addTypingIndicator() {
      const wrap = document.createElement("article");
      wrap.className = "message-wrap assistant";

      const card = document.createElement("div");
      card.className = "message assistant";

      const meta = document.createElement("div");
      meta.className = "message-meta";
      meta.innerHTML = "<span>Iris</span><span>" + timestamp() + "</span>";

      const body = document.createElement("div");
      body.className = "message-body";
      body.innerHTML = '<div class="typing" aria-label="Iris is thinking"><span></span><span></span><span></span> Iris is thinking...</div>';

      card.appendChild(meta);
      card.appendChild(body);
      wrap.appendChild(card);
      chatLog.appendChild(wrap);
      scrollChat();
      return { wrap, body };
    }

    function prismStateMessage(hardware) {
      const nics = Array.isArray(hardware.nics) ? hardware.nics : [];
      const extraDisks = Array.isArray(hardware.extra_disks) ? hardware.extra_disks : [];
      const gpuDevices = Array.isArray(hardware.gpu_devices) ? hardware.gpu_devices : [];
      const nvidiaGpus = Array.isArray(hardware.nvidia_gpus) ? hardware.nvidia_gpus : [];
      const diskSummary = extraDisks.length
        ? extraDisks.map((disk) => [disk.name, disk.path, disk.size, disk.model].filter(Boolean).join(" ")).join(" | ")
        : "none reported";
      const gpuSummary = gpuDevices.length
        ? gpuDevices.map((gpu) => gpu.description || JSON.stringify(gpu)).join(" | ")
        : "none reported";
      const nvidiaSummary = nvidiaGpus.length
        ? nvidiaGpus.map((gpu) => JSON.stringify(gpu)).join(" | ")
        : "nvidia_gpus field missing or empty";

      return [
        "PRISM_STATE below is the only source of truth for local PRISM hardware, setup, model, backend, and service state.",
        "You may only report local system facts that appear in PRISM_STATE or in explicit tool results.",
        "Never invent hardware.",
        "Never invent service status.",
        "Never invent files, logs, command output, installation results, job results, or port numbers.",
        "Never claim you ran a command unless a real tool result is provided.",
        "Never provide sample command output as if it came from this machine.",
        "If a field is missing from PRISM_STATE, say you do not have that information.",
        "If PRISM_STATE is unavailable, stale, empty, or invalid, say: \"I do not currently have verified PRISM hardware or service state available.\"",
        "If asked where information came from, say: \"From PRISM_STATE fetched from /setup/state.\"",
        "Report uncertainty plainly. Do not guess.",
        "Use this verified summary when answering hardware questions. It is derived directly from PRISM_STATE and must not be embellished.",
        "Do not report MAC addresses or disk serial numbers unless the user explicitly asks for them.",
        "setup_complete: " + hardware.setup_complete,
        "total_ram_mb: " + hardware.total_ram_mb,
        "nic_count: " + (Number.isFinite(hardware.nic_count) ? hardware.nic_count : nics.length),
        "extra_disks_count: " + extraDisks.length,
        "extra_disks: " + diskSummary,
        "gpu_present: " + hardware.gpu_present,
        "gpu_usable: " + hardware.gpu_usable,
        "gpu_driver: " + (hardware.gpu_driver || "missing"),
        "gpu_devices_count: " + gpuDevices.length,
        "gpu_devices: " + gpuSummary,
        "nvidia_gpus: " + nvidiaSummary,
        "recommended_model: " + (hardware.recommended_model || "missing"),
        "ollama_model_installed: " + hardware.ollama_model_installed,
        "ollama_gpu_ready: " + hardware.ollama_gpu_ready,
        "PRISM_STATE:",
        JSON.stringify(hardware)
      ].join("\n");
    }

    function normalizeHardwareState(hardware) {
      const totalRamMb = hardware.total_ram_mb || hardware.ram_mb || 0;
      const nics = Array.isArray(hardware.nics) ? hardware.nics : [];
      const extraDisks = Array.isArray(hardware.extra_disks) ? hardware.extra_disks : [];
      const gpuDetected = Boolean(hardware.gpu_present || hardware.gpu_detected || hardware.gpu_usable);

      return {
        totalRamMb,
        ramGb: totalRamMb ? (totalRamMb / 1024).toFixed(1) : "unknown",
        extraDiskCount: extraDisks.length,
        gpuDetected,
        nicCount: hardware.nic_count || nics.length,
        recommendedModel: hardware.recommended_model || "unknown"
      };
    }

    async function detectMode() {
      // Setup mode is detected by the presence of the setup backend. If the backend
      // is absent or unreachable, the same UI falls back to normal assistant mode.
      try {
        const response = await fetch("/setup/state", { method: "GET" });
        if (!response.ok) {
          throw new Error("setup backend returned " + response.status);
        }

        const hardware = await response.json();
        const normalized = normalizeHardwareState(hardware);
        setMode("setup");

        setStatus([
          "Detected mode: setup",
          "RAM: " + normalized.totalRamMb + "MB (" + normalized.ramGb + "GB)",
          "Extra disks: " + normalized.extraDiskCount,
          "GPU detected: " + (normalized.gpuDetected ? "yes" : "no"),
          "NICs: " + normalized.nicCount,
          "Recommended model: " + normalized.recommendedModel
        ]);

        return hardware;
      } catch (_error) {
        setMode("normal");
        setStatus([
          "Detected mode: normal",
          "Setup backend not detected",
          "Using local Iris assistant prompt",
          "Ollama API expected at /api/chat"
        ]);
        return null;
      }
    }

    async function streamChat() {
      const response = await fetch("/api/chat", {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          model: currentModel,
          stream: true,
          messages: messages
        })
      });

      if (!response.ok || !response.body) {
        throw new Error("chat request failed: " + response.status);
      }

      const typing = addTypingIndicator();
      const reader = response.body.getReader();
      const decoder = new TextDecoder();
      let raw = "";
      let assistantText = "";
      let firstChunk = true;
      let assistantBody = null;

      while (true) {
        const { value, done } = await reader.read();
        if (done) {
          break;
        }

        raw += decoder.decode(value, { stream: true });
        const lines = raw.split("\n");
        raw = lines.pop() || "";

        for (const line of lines) {
          const trimmed = line.trim();
          if (!trimmed) {
            continue;
          }

          const payload = JSON.parse(trimmed);
          const fragment = payload.message && payload.message.content ? payload.message.content : "";
          if (!fragment) {
            continue;
          }

          if (firstChunk) {
            typing.body.textContent = "";
            assistantBody = typing.body;
            firstChunk = false;
          }

          assistantText += fragment;
          assistantBody.textContent = assistantText;
          scrollChat();
        }
      }

      if (firstChunk) {
        typing.wrap.remove();
        addMessage("assistant", "Iris", "Iris did not return a visible response.");
        messages.push({ role: "assistant", content: "Iris did not return a visible response." });
      } else {
        messages.push({ role: "assistant", content: assistantText.trim() });
      }
    }

    async function bootConversation(hardware) {
      if (currentMode === "setup" && hardware) {
        const normalized = normalizeHardwareState(hardware);
        const bootPrompt = [
          "PRISM Net first boot has started.",
          "Detected hardware:",
          normalized.ramGb + "GB RAM,",
          normalized.extraDiskCount + " extra disks,",
          (normalized.gpuDetected ? "GPU present," : "no GPU,"),
          normalized.nicCount + " network interfaces.",
          "Introduce yourself in one sentence, explain PRISM simply, summarize the hardware, and offer exactly two choices: Just set it up or Let me choose."
        ].join(" ");

        addMessage("system", "PRISM", "Setup backend detected. Iris is entering first-boot setup mode.");
        messages.push({ role: "system", content: currentPrompt });
        messages.push({ role: "system", content: prismStateMessage(hardware) });
        messages.push({ role: "user", content: bootPrompt });
        addMessage("user", "System Boot", bootPrompt);
        await streamChat();
        return;
      }

      try {
        const response = await fetch("/setup/state", { method: "GET" });
        if (response.ok) {
          const hardware = await response.json();
          messages.push({ role: "system", content: prismStateMessage(hardware) });
        }
      } catch (_error) {
        // Normal mode must still work when the setup backend is absent.
      }

      const normalPrompt = "Introduce yourself as Iris in one sentence, explain that this is PRISM, and ask how you can help with this private home server.";
      addMessage("system", "PRISM", "Setup backend not detected. Iris is using the normal assistant prompt.");
      messages.push({ role: "system", content: currentPrompt });
      messages.push({ role: "user", content: normalPrompt });
      addMessage("user", "System Boot", normalPrompt);
      await streamChat();
    }

    chatForm.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      const text = chatInput.value.trim();
      if (!text) {
        return;
      }

      chatInput.value = "";
      sendButton.disabled = true;
      addMessage("user", "You", text);
      messages.push({ role: "user", content: text });

      try {
        await streamChat();
      } catch (error) {
        addMessage("system", "Error", "Iris could not respond: " + error.message);
      } finally {
        sendButton.disabled = false;
        chatInput.focus();
      }
    });

    chatInput.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
      if (event.key === "Enter" && !event.shiftKey) {
        event.preventDefault();
        chatForm.requestSubmit();
      }
    });

    async function init() {
      const hardware = await detectMode();
      try {
        await bootConversation(hardware);
      } catch (error) {
        addMessage("system", "Error", "Startup failed: " + error.message);
      }
      chatInput.focus();
    }

    init();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
